rom the stack which item is at the top of stack.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> S</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> T</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> U</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> R</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/73018db4c1c379bcec1874da0fbf2c60203eb070.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following statements (or) expressions is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/cf391b7e19a8af5f9f6869f59573fd9bb24fd6d6.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/aaa70dcbe18b68443cbbf2563fe702cba6e5e185.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> malloc( ) always by default returns integer pointer when memory is allocated</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> type casting is not required when memory allocated by using malloc( )</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, c)<br />\n(a) p is a pointer to a function that takes and argument as pointer to a character array and returns a pointer to an integer.<br />\n(c) malloc( ) always by default returns integer pointer when memory is allocated.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The key 32, 14, 28, 22, 5, 3, 19, 42, 33, 48, 24, 27 are inserted into an initially sized hash table of length 8 using hash function h(k) = k mod 8 and the collision resolution are resolved by chaining. Calculate the number keys suffer from collision that can occur and the maximum chain length size.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> (5, 4)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> (5, 3)</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> (5, 2)</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> (5, 0)</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/fad1fcaede92c5e579c3f2b1c6de1535725b2829.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : A key has to be inserted in table of size ‘<em>n</em>’ having ‘<em>k</em>’ items by using a hash function. The probability of hitting a free location in the first time is<img src=\"/media/7f5aa57186e2ec9b4cc665410839e1003f751b68.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" />resolved using linear probing.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : In hash function using linear probing to reduce collision, the number of probes required to insert an item is identical with number of probes needed to retrieve it.<br />\nThe number of statement correct are ________.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2","high":"2"},"solution":"<p>2</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/b633bc441b0ac0cbc3540d11a398b8acbc2828a1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A multi-dimensional array <img src=\"/media/a049160611a0da5e832c7d0f37a907040f66c409.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is same as</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/5b68878f7ca24a1d7844793ebbafd4b1b38f6e2c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/1af248a74f71ced9f95f56ea9328dfadbcf556d6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/bc15513d380274a6b8c378756bcdceb1dfec8cb3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)<